{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792336518,"nonce":"yOXPwi0rll5Hw2FbQATVK3fPEJc=","title":"Hybrid at --jit-threshold 1: a conformance case sometimes exits 0 with no test output","message":"Seen three times in gate runs of the unit conformance suite with every function compiled at its first call (hybrid, `--jit-threshold 1`, isolated cases): unit.TestExceptions reported FAIL in one run, and unit.issues.Issue1845 reported CRASH in another with `exit 0 without a tally; last line: Interpreter returned: Void` after 48 ms. The next gates were clean.\n\nThe one failing run I could capture by hand (60 sequential runs of Issue1845 with main's binary, 10d8b19b) printed only the three `[ash] Loading HDLL` lines on stderr and the trailer `Interpreter returned: Void`; stdout, where the utest report goes, was empty and the exit status 0. A good run prints the report ending `results: ALL TESTS OK`. The same binary failed 0 of 200 sequential runs, 0 of 400 at 12 in parallel and 0 of 3000 at 6 in parallel afterwards, and the branch with the collector changes failed 0 of 60, so the rate is about one in several thousand and not tied to that change.\n\nCandidates not yet checked: stdout bytes written by the program thread not flushed when the process ends while the promoter or a compile thread is running (the threshold makes every function a compile job), or the harness losing a pipe read. To catch it: loop the case with stdout redirected to a file and keep any run whose file lacks `results:`; the case is `unit/bin/unit.hl --ash-only unit.issues.Issue1845` from ~/.cache/ash-haxe-conformance/haxe-tests-4.3.6/tests.","files":null}]}